1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,640
Okay and if after hearing all of this you're still thinking well it's not that I've never been loved it's just that I've never had that one person I can call mine.
好，如果听完这些，你仍想说：并不是从没被爱过，只是从没有那个能称为自己伴侣的人，

2
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:14,720
Then we are talking about a different type of loneliness now okay.
那么，我们现在谈的是另一种孤独。

3
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:20,069
One that stems less from lack and more from desire.
一种与其说来自缺失，不如说来自渴望的孤独，

4
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:25,840
Sometimes even from the fantasy and stories we've been fed about what love is supposed to look like.
有时甚至来自那些灌输给我们的幻想和故事，告诉我们爱“应该”是什么样子。

5
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,959
And that kind of ache is valid by the way.
顺便说，这种隐痛也是真实、值得被承认的。

6
00:00:28,959 --> 00:00:35,680
It's valid it can be just as sharp and just as consuming as the ones that come from actual lack.
它也可能像真正缺失带来的痛一样尖锐、一样占据心神。

7
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:40,400
But it's important to call it what it is romantic relationships are not guarantees.
不过，作者认为，需要说清楚：恋爱关系并不是必然会得到的。

8
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:44,150
They are not owed they are not fundamental human rights.
她继续说，它们不是别人欠你的，也不是基本人权。

9
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:48,960
So their absence in your life is not a failure it's not proof that something is wrong with you.
所以，她认为生活中没有伴侣，不是失败，也不说明你有什么问题。

10
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:57,200
Yes desires are human but they don't define your worth and they certainly don't have to dictate the quality of your life okay.
渴望很人性化，但它不定义你的价值，也不必决定你的生活质量。

11
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,120
My video the search for the one might be very beneficial to you.
她提到，自己另一条谈寻找伴侣的视频，也许会对你有帮助。

12
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:10,230
Maybe your loneliness comes from the absence of family maybe you feel the gap during hard times you know when other people call their moms or rely on their dads.
也许你的孤独来自家庭缺位，尤其困难时，看别人给妈妈打电话、依靠爸爸，

13
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,640
And you have no one you trust enough to call.
而你却没有一个足够信任、可以打电话的人。

14
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:18,800
Or maybe your parents or your loved ones have passed on and you're carrying the weight of that loss in silence or alone.
或者父母、所爱之人已经离世，你独自、默默承受失去的重量。

15
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:26,520
Or maybe you're one of the many humans with divergent minds trying to survive in a world built on neurocformity.
也许，你属于思维方式不同的人，努力在一个偏向思维一致的世界生活；最后一词识别不清。

16
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:32,160
In that case your loneliness isn't imagined it's it's it's systemic.
在她看来，这样的孤独并非想象，而可能与社会系统有关。

17
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:35,840
You may be surrounded by people who love you people who show up for you.
你可能被爱你、愿意支持你的人包围，

18
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:40,390
And still feel like there's a pane of glass between you and the rest of the world.
但依然像隔着一层玻璃，横在你与其余世界之间。

19
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,800
Like you're close but never quite reached seen but never quite understood.
像是很近，却没有真正被触及；被看见，却没有被真正理解。

20
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:50,480
And that kind of loneliness it's not about being alone it's not about you know it's not about proximity.
她说，这样的孤独不只是独自一人，也不只是空间距离的问题。

21
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:56,400
It's about being misread misuned and emotionally mistransated again and again.
而是一次又一次被误读、未被调频般地理解、在情感上被错译；后两词自动识别待核。

22
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:04,869
In ways so normalized so deeply embedded in our culture in the fabric of our cultures our institutions into everyday expectations.
这些方式被视为寻常，深深嵌入文化、制度，以及日常期待里，

23
00:02:04,879 --> 00:02:07,999
That most people don't even notice that it's happening.
以至于许多人甚至没注意到它在发生。

24
00:02:07,999 --> 00:02:13,830
This can also apply to people who are culturally or racially distinct in the spaces they occupy.
她说，这也可能适用于在所处环境中文化或种族背景不同的人。

25
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:17,040
Telling you to get a new hobby isn't the answer certainly.
仅仅让你找个新爱好，当然未必就能解决。

26
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:22,950
So maybe your relief can come from actively seeking spaces made out for mind like minds like yours.
所以，她建议可以主动寻找适合类似思维方式的空间；原声有自我修正。

27
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:29,360
Sensory safe environments or even communities where people speak your rhythm or share your culture.
适合感官需要的环境，或者节奏与你相近、文化与你相通的社群。

28
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,520
The reason I'm asking you to identify the exact causes of your loneliness.
我请你辨认孤独的具体原因，

29
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:37,680
Is so that you can deal with it in a targeted and mindful way.
是希望你能有针对性、有觉察地应对。

30
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:44,640
Because if what you're craving is emotional connection then physical closeness that lacks that emotional depth won't help.
因为若你渴望的是情感联结，那么缺乏情感深度的身体接近，未必能帮到你。

31
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:48,080
It will keep you visibly not alone but internally empty.
它可能让你表面上不是一个人，内心却仍空空的。

32
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:54,470
That's like trying to treat cancer with painkillers it might numb the ache but it won't kill those cells.
她借癌症与止痛药作比喻：也许缓和疼痛，却未处理病灶；这里只转述比喻，不作为治疗知识。

33
00:02:54,480 --> 00:03:01,190
This is why so many of us are waste deep in painful relationships unhealthy attachments and shallow connections.
她认为，这解释了为何有人深陷痛苦关系、不健康依恋和浅层联结，

34
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:07,040
Because we aren't willing to sit with our ache long enough to learn what it might mean.
因为我们不愿与那种隐痛相处足够久，去了解它可能意味着什么。

35
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,439
And what will it mean what does it mean.
那它会意味着什么，又是什么呢？这里保留作者反复追问的停顿。

36
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:17,680
It means accepting that some kinds of loneliness might never fully go away especially the systemic kind.
她说，也许要承认某些孤独不会完全消失，特别是她所说的系统性孤独，

37
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:23,280
Or that healing them might take time or truth or a whole lot of discomfort.
或者，要缓解它，需要时间、诚实面对自己，以及许多不适感。
